      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FLASH BOOM BANG (1) is a quick dog who thrives over the short dashes. Was too tough when scoring last time over 400m at Bulli in a Grade 4/5 (22.43). Form at the trip excellent including two wins. Comes out of a solid form race last start. Well placed and can measure up. PAPER SHREDDER (8) has a fair record and proved too strong last time to win by 1.5 lengths at The Gardens in a handy 22.93 beating Stock's Gift. Ran one of the fastest times on the program in his latest win. Makes plenty of appeal if runs up to latest. GREAT FLASH (3) turned in a plain performance last time when sixth at The Gardens over 400m behind PAPER SHREDDER (23.41) in a Mix 1/2/3. Was in the money prior to that. Good beginner aided by a nice draw. Better than last start and can bounce back. TULSI BANNER (5) is worth a look despite no experience at this circuit.",
